# DURABLE control-authority surfaces only (Architecture A / RC-453 / RC-459).
#
# "Durable" = a file that can flip the required CI verdict (the only two required
# gates, .github/workflows/hardening.yml + pytest.yml) or the review policy itself,
# such that a boundary-broken state could merge CI-green with NO operator review.
# That is: the import closure of the hardening gate scripts (a weakened check merges
# green — the delta gate detects a REMOVED check, not silently-weakened logic), every
# conftest.py (a poisoned one fakes the whole suite green), the PM-authority mechanism,
# tools/__init__.py, and the Architecture-A definition tests.
#
# NARROWED (RC-459, operator-ratified 2026-08-23): local-only hook wiring
# (.cursor/hooks.json, .claude/settings.json, .pre-commit-config.yaml), pre-commit
# wrappers, and ~20 standalone non-hardening check_*.py are DEFENSE-IN-DEPTH, not the
# durable boundary — poisoning them, if merged, changes only local behavior, not the CI
# verdict or the OS boundary — so they are intentionally NOT listed and do not force
# operator review. Ordinary product paths (server.py, db.py, static/, signals.py,
# models) are likewise NOT listed so the assigned AI lands ordinary work autonomously.
# A self-maintaining test (tests/test_control_authority_surfaces_v1.py) recomputes the
# CI-verdict closure and FAILS if a gate script gains an un-owned import.

